{"cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\\\\nusing namespace std;\\\\nint main() {\\\\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\\\\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\\\\n    int n, k;\\\\n    if (!(cin >> n >> k)) return 0;\\\\n    vector<int> arr(n);\\\\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> arr[i];\\\\n    deque<int> dq;\\\\n    vector<int> result;\\\\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\\\\n        if (!dq.empty() && dq.front() + k <= i) {\\\\n            dq.pop_front();\\\\n        }\\\\n        while (!dq.empty() && arr[dq.back()] <= arr[i]) {\\\\n            dq.pop_back();\\\\n        }\\\\n        dq.push_back(i);\\\\n        if (i >= k - 1) {\\\\n            result.push_back(arr[dq.front()]);\\\\n        }\\\\n    }\\\\n    for (int i = 0; i < (int)result.size(); i++) {\\\\n        cout << result[i] << (i == (int)result.size() - 1 ? \\"\\" : \\" \\");\\\\n    }\\\\n    cout << \\"\\\\\\\\n\\";\\\\n    return 0;\\\\n}"}	2026-07-03 07:10:28.305	2026-07-03 07:10:28.305
126a4bf2-e7c3-4166-a4fe-429de00b4d56	H-Index	Given an array of integers citations where citations[i] is the number of citations a researcher received for their i-th paper, return the researcher's h-index.\n\nThe h-index is defined as the maximum value of h such that the given researcher has published at least h papers that have each been cited at least h times.\n\n**Input Format:**\n- First line: integer N\n- Second line: N space-separated integers representing citations\n\n**Output Format:**\n- A single integer representing the researcher's h-index	MEDIUM	{sorting}	ccf6772f-27d4-4001-bd5e-763e3c380ba0	[{"input": "5\\n3 0 6 1 5", "title": "Example 1", "output": "3", "explanation": "The researcher has 5 papers in total. 3 papers have at least 3 citations each (3, 5, 6)."}, {"input": "3\\n1 3 1", "title": "Example 2", "output": "1", "explanation": "Only 1 paper has at least 1 citation."}]	1 <= N <= 10^5\n0 <= citations[i] <= 10^9	Sort the citations array in ascending order. If citations[i] >= N - i, then we have at least N - i papers with citations >= citations[i].	**Approach: Sorting**\n\nSort citations in ascending order. For each paper at index i, the number of papers with at least citations[i] citations is N - i. We find the maximum value of N - i such that citations[i] >= N - i.\n\n**Time Complexity:** O(N log N)\n**Space Complexity:** O(1) or O(N) depending on the sort algorithm	[{"input": "5\\n3 0 6 1 5", "output": "3"}, {"input": "3\\n1 3 1", "output": "1"}, {"input": "1\\n0", "output": "0"}, {"input": "1\\n100", "output": "1"}, {"input": "5\\n10 8 5 4 3", "output": "4"}, {"input": "4\\n0 0 0 0", "output": "0"}, {"input": "6\\n10 10 10 10 10 10", "output": "6"}, {"input": "5\\n1 1 1 1 1", "output": "1"}, {"input": "5\\n2 2 2 2 2", "output": "2"}, {"input": "7\\n4 0 5 1 6 3 2", "output": "3"}, {"input": "5\\n0 0 0 0", "output": "0"}, {"input": "17\\n14 10 15 11 16 13 12", "output": "7"}, {"input": "60\\n7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 