"input": "0 0\\n-1 -2 -2\\n-3 -2 -2\\n-2 -3 -2", "output": "0"}, {"input": "4 4\\n2 0 2", "output": "0"}]	{"cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\\nusing namespace std;\\nint main() { return 0; }"}	{"cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\\nusing namespace std;\\nint main() {\\n    int r, c; if (!(cin >> r >> c)) return 0;\\n    vector<vector<int>> g(r, vector<int>(c));\\n    queue<pair<int, int>> q; int fresh = 0;\\n    for (int i = 0; i < r; i++) {\\n        for (int j = 0; j < c; j++) {\\n            cin >> g[i][j];\\n            if (g[i][j] == 2) q.push({i, j});\\n            else if (g[i][j] == 1) fresh++;\\n        }\\n    }\\n    int mins = 0;\\n    int dr[] = {-1, 1, 0, 0}, dc[] = {0, 0, -1, 1};\\n    while (!q.empty() && fresh > 0) {\\n        int sz = q.size(); mins++;\\n        for (int i = 0; i < sz; i++) {\\n            auto [cr, cc] = q.front(); q.pop();\\n            for (int d = 0; d < 4; d++) {\\n                int nr = cr + dr[d], nc = cc + dc[d];\\n                if (nr >= 0 && nr < r && nc >= 0 && nc < c && g[nr][nc] == 1) {\\n                    g[nr][nc] = 2; fresh--; q.push({nr, nc});\\n                }\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n    cout << (fresh == 0 ? mins : -1) << \\"\\\\n\\";\\n}"}	2026-07-03 07:10:28.493	2026-07-03 07:10:28.493
f5f7cad1-b201-4ed2-a2ea-151a1d79ec48	Dijkstra Shortest Path	Given a weighted, undirected connected graph with N vertices (labeled 0 to N-1) and M edges, and a source vertex S. Find the shortest distance from the source vertex S to all other vertices in the graph. If a vertex is unreachable, the distance should be -1.\n\n**Input Format:**\n- First line: N M S\n- Next M lines: u v w (undirected edge between u and v with weight w)\n\n**Output Format:**\n- A single line of space-separated integers representing the shortest distance from source S to vertices 0 to N-1.	MEDIUM	{graphs,shortest-path}	ccf6772f-27d4-4001-bd5e-763e3c380ba0	[{"input": "4 4 0\\n0 1 1\\n1 2 2\\n2 3 3\\n0 3 5", "title": "Example 1", "output": "0 1 3 5"}, {"input": "3 2 1\\n0 1 5\\n1 2 2", "title": "Example 2", "output": "5 0 2"}]	1 <= N <= 10^4\n0 <= M <= 5 * 10^4\n0 <= S < N\n1 <= w <= 10^4\n0 <= u, v < N	Use a min-priority queue to perform Dijkstra\\'s algorithm. Maintain a distance array initialized to infinity, with distance to S set to 0.	Initialize the shortest path values as infinity for all nodes, except S which is 0. Push {0, S} to the min-priority queue. While the priority queue is not empty, extract the node u with the minimum distance. If the distance in queue is greater than the recorded distance, skip. Otherwise, for each neighbor v with weight w, if dist[u] + w < dist[v], update dist[v] and push {dist[v], v} to the queue. Finally, print the distances, converting any unreachable vertex distance (still infinity) to -1.	[{"input": "4 4 0\\n0 1 1\\n1 2 2\\n2 3 3\\n0 3 5", "output": "0 1 3 5"}, {"input": "3 2 1\\n0 1 5\\n1 2 2", "output": "5 0 2"}, {"input": "1 0 0", "output": "0"}, {"input": "4 3 3\\n0 1 10\\n1 2 20\\n2 3 30", "output": "60 50 30 0"}, {"input": "5 6 0\\n0 1 2\\n0 2 4\\n1 2 1\\n1 3 7\\n2 4 3\\n3 4 1", "output": "0 2 3 9 6"}, {"input": "5 4 0\\n0 1 10\\n0 2 10\\n3 4 5\\n0 0 1", "output": "0 10 10 -1 -1"}, {"input": "4 2 2\\n0 1 1\\n2 3 5", "output": "-1 -1 0 5"}, {"input"