r (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {\\n        int u, v, w;\\n        cin >> u >> v >> w;\\n        adj[u].push_back({v, w});\\n        adj[v].push_back({u, w});\\n    }\\n    vector<int> dist(n, INF);\\n    dist[s] = 0;\\n    priority_queue<pair<int, int>, vector<pair<int, int>>, greater<pair<int, int>>> pq;\\n    pq.push({0, s});\\n    while (!pq.empty()) {\\n        auto [d, u] = pq.top();\\n        pq.pop();\\n        if (d > dist[u]) continue;\\n        for (auto& edge : adj[u]) {\\n            int v = edge.first;\\n            int w = edge.second;\\n            if (dist[u] + w < dist[v]) {\\n                dist[v] = dist[u] + w;\\n                pq.push({dist[v], v});\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\\n        int val = (dist[i] == INF ? -1 : dist[i]);\\n        cout << val << (i + 1 == n ? \\"\\" : \\" \\");\\n    }\\n    cout << \\"\\\\n\\";\\n    return 0;\\n}"}	2026-07-03 07:10:28.5	2026-07-03 07:10:28.5
daca2c3a-c720-462d-95bf-e403b92ee76a	Coin Change	You are given an integer array coins representing coins of different denominations and an integer amount representing a total amount of money.\n\nReturn the fewest number of coins that you need to make up that amount. If that amount of money cannot be made up by any combination of the coins, return -1.\n\nYou may assume that you have an infinite number of each kind of coin.\n\n**Input Format:**\n- First line: two space-separated integers n and amount (where n is the number of coins)\n- Second line: n space-separated integers representing the coin denominations\n\n**Output Format:**\n- A single integer: the minimum number of coins needed, or -1.	MEDIUM	{dynamic-programming,tabulation}	ccf6772f-27d4-4001-bd5e-763e3c380ba0	[{"input": "3 11\\n1 2 5", "title": "Example 1", "output": "3", "explanation": "11 = 5 + 5 + 1"}, {"input": "1 3\\n2", "title": "Example 2", "output": "-1"}]	1 <= n <= 12\n1 <= coins[i] <= 2^31 - 1\n0 <= amount <= 10^4	Let dp[i] represent the minimum number of coins to make up amount i. To calculate dp[i], check all coins c: dp[i] = min(dp[i], dp[i-c] + 1).	**Approach: 1D DP (Tabulation)**\n\nLet `dp[i]` be the minimum coins to make amount `i`.\nInitialize `dp[0] = 0` and all other elements to `amount + 1`.\nFor `i` from 1 to `amount`:\n  For each coin `c` in `coins`:\n     if `i >= c`:\n       `dp[i] = min(dp[i], dp[i - c] + 1)`\n\nIf `dp[amount]` remains `amount + 1`, it is impossible to make that amount, so return -1.\n\n**Time Complexity:** O(amount * n)\n**Space Complexity:** O(amount)	[{"input": "3 11\\n1 2 5", "output": "3"}, {"input": "1 3\\n2", "output": "-1"}, {"input": "1 0\\n1", "output": "0"}, {"input": "4 0\\n1 2 5 10", "output": "0"}, {"input": "2 3\\n2 4", "output": "-1"}, {"input": "3 100\\n1 2 5", "output": "20"}, {"input": "4 6249\\n186 419 83 408", "output": "20"}, {"input": "5 120\\n10 20 30 40 50", "output": "3"}, {"input": "1 10000\\n1", "output": "10000"}, {"input": "3 11\\n2 5 